A. PROBLEM STATEMENT

Design Low-Level Design for Library Management System.

Requirements:

Users (Members) can register, search books, issue books, and return books.
Librarians can add/remove books, manage members, and track issued books.
Support book search by title, author, or category.
Handle due dates, fines for late returns.
Prevent issuing already issued books.
Maintain transaction history.

Constraints:

In-memory implementation is acceptable.
Support multiple members and books.

Edge Cases:

Book already issued.
Member has reached max borrow limit.
Late return (fine calculation).
Book not found.

